[B][COLOR=#00bfff] Configuring item pricing[/COLOR][/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]Open the entry file[/B]: Each category lives under [icode]plugins/EzShops/shop/categories/[/icode]; edit the item section (for example [icode]farming.yml[/icode] ➝ [icode]wheat_seeds[/icode]).
[*][B]Set your base totals[/B]: Update the [icode]buy[/icode] and [icode]sell[/icode] values to control the price for the configured [icode]amount[/icode]; EzShops scales shift-click totals for you, and [icode]bulk-amount[/icode] changes the alternative stack size.
[*][B]Enable dynamic swings[/B]: Add an optional [icode]dynamic-pricing[/icode] block with [icode]enabled[/icode], [icode]starting-multiplier[/icode], [icode]min-multiplier[/icode], [icode]max-multiplier[/icode], [icode]buy-change[/icode], and [icode]sell-change[/icode] to let prices respond automatically to trades.
[*][B]Apply changes[/B]: Save the file and reload EzShops (or restart the server) to push the updated numbers live to menus, signs, and API consumers.
[/LIST]
[code=yaml]
wheat_seeds:
  material: WHEAT_SEEDS
  slot: 10
  amount: 16
  bulk-amount: 64
  buy: 15.0
  sell: 3.8
  dynamic-pricing:
    enabled: true
    starting-multiplier: 1.0
    min-multiplier: 0.7
    max-multiplier: 2.1
    buy-change: 0.018
    sell-change: 0.012
[/code]

[B][COLOR=#00bfff] Configuring rotating specials[/COLOR][/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]Define the schedule[/B]: Edit plugins/EzShops/shop/rotations/daily-specials.yml (or create a new file under shop/rotations/). Set interval to an ISO-8601 duration like PT6H or compact shorthand such as 6h, choose a mode of sequential or random, and pick a default-option for fresh installs.
[*][B]Wire the category[/B]: Point rotation-group inside the matching category file (the bundle ships shop/categories/daily_specials.yml). The optional rotation-defaults block supplies the shared icon, menu title, and baseline item data that every option inherits.
[*][B]Override per option[/B]: Inside each option’s items block, override only the fields you need (material, prices, amounts, lore, or icons). Add weight values when using random mode to bias how often each option appears.
[*][B]Reload and monitor[/B]: Reload EzShops or restart the server. The plugin copies active selections to shop-rotations.yml so admins can track timers or pin a specific option between rotations.
[/LIST]
[code=yaml]
rotations:
  daily-specials:
    interval: 12h
    mode: random
    default-option: farming-frenzy
    options:
      farming-frenzy:
        menu-title: '&aDaily Special: Farming Frenzy'
      monster-madness:
        weight: 2
        items:
          harvest_bundle:
            material: ROTTEN_FLESH
            buy: 24.0
            sell: 9.5
[/code]

[B][COLOR=#00bfff] Sign shops[/COLOR][/B]
[IMG]https://i.ibb.co/0RFSYmLC/ez-shops-sign-shops.png[/IMG]
[LIST]
[*][B]Mirror menu offers[/B]: Tie a sign to any priced [icode]Material[/icode]; EzShops pulls the same buy/sell data used by your GUI entries.
[*][B]Quick setup[/B]: Place [icode][shop][/icode] on line one, [icode]buy[/icode] or [icode]sell[/icode] on line two, the item (for example [icode]DIAMOND_BLOCK[/icode]) on line three, and the stack amount on line four.
[*][B]Example layout[/B]: [icode][shop][/icode] / [icode]buy[/icode] / [icode]DIAMOND_BLOCK[/icode] / [icode]1[/icode] instantly rewrites to your themed header, action text, item name, and formatted price.
[*][B]Granular permissions[/B]: Lock creation behind [icode]ezshops.shop.sign.create[/icode] while letting standard shop permissions govern who can buy or sell through the sign.
[*][B]Player feedback[/B]: Players receive chat confirmations while the sign updates its colored price line after each trade.
[*][B]Batch generator GUI[/B]: Run [icode]/signshop[/icode] (permission [icode]ezshops.shop.sign.setup[/icode]) to open a planner GUI that pulls items from your inventory, flips between buy/sell modes, sets a shared backing block, tweaks spacing and rows, and chains together as many synchronized signs as you need before confirmation.
[IMG]https://i.ibb.co/0RLw862m/ez-shops-sign-setup-gui.png[/IMG]
[*][B]One-click placement[/B]: Look at the block you want behind the first sign and hit confirm; EzShops lays down the backing line and wall signs in front of you using your configured formatting, stack sizes, and stored metadata so they trade immediately.
[/LIST]

[B][COLOR=#00bfff] How to use the sign shop generator[/COLOR][/B]
[LIST=1]
[*][B]Open the planner[/B]: Run [icode]/signshop[/icode] (permission [icode]ezshops.shop.sign.setup[/icode]) to open the generator GUI and pull eligible materials from your inventory.
[*][B]Select your template item[/B]: Click an item in your inventory pane to add it to the plan. EzShops copies its material, display name, lore, and buy/sell prices straight from the linked menu entry.
[*][B]Choose buy or sell mode[/B]: Use the toggle buttons to decide whether every generated sign handles purchases or sales, and set the stack amount if you need something other than the default.
[*][B]Configure the layout[/B]: Pick the backing block, adjust spacing and row count, and preview the final sign text so you know exactly how the strip will look in-game.
[*][B]Confirm placement[/B]: Stand where you want the line to begin, look at the supporting block, and press the confirm item; EzShops places the backing and every formatted sign using the plan you just saved.
[*][B]Reuse saved plans[/B]: The generator keeps your last configuration so you can rerun [icode]/signshop[/icode], tweak a detail, and redeploy another set of synchronized buy or sell signs in seconds.
[/LIST]

[B][COLOR=#00bfff] Scanning sign shops[/COLOR][/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]/signshop scan[/B]: Sweep the nearby area for EzShops-formatted signs and highlight any that no longer match their linked GUI entry or have invalid headers.
[*][B]Permission gated[/B]: Limit the audit tool to trusted staff with [icode]ezshops.shop.sign.scan[/icode] so regular players can’t spam alerts.
[*][B]Instant feedback[/B]: Scans summarize the number of corrected signs, orphaned headers, or skipped locations right in chat so you know where to investigate.
[*][B]One-click fixes[/B]: Choose the optional autofix prompt to rewrite outdated lines, reapply pricing, and restore proper formatting without touching each sign manually.
[*][B]Perfect for expansions[/B]: Run a scan after big layout changes or world edits to ensure every strip still points at a valid backing block before opening your new district.
[/LIST]

[B][COLOR=#00bfff] Player shops[/COLOR][/B]
[IMG]https://i.ibb.co/6cWJNW5w/ez-shops-player-setup.png[/IMG]
[IMG]https://i.ibb.co/bjsBpvpN/ez-shops-player-shop-sign.png[/IMG]
[LIST]
[*][B]Let the community sell[/B]: Players place [icode][playershop][/icode] on a sign attached to their chest, add the quantity and price (or reuse saved defaults), and EzShops validates the stock before activating the listing.
[*][B]Automatic formatting[/B]: Successful shops rewrite their signs with color-coded headers, owner names, item summaries, and price lines that reflect stock status.
[*][B]Offline earnings[/B]: Purchases withdraw money from buyers, deposit it into the owner's account, and send notifications when the seller is online.
[*][B]Secure storage[/B]: Only owners (or admins with [icode]ezshops.playershop.admin[/icode]) can break signs or open connected chests, preventing grief and theft.
[*][B]Permission tiers[/B]: Grant [icode]ezshops.playershop.create[/icode] to trusted builders, [icode]ezshops.playershop.buy[/icode] to the wider community, and reserve [icode]ezshops.playershop.admin[/icode] for staff oversight.
[*][B]Configurable rules[/B]: Require stocked chests, clamp quantity or pricing ranges, or disable the feature entirely using the [icode]player-shops[/icode] block inside [icode]config.yml[/icode].
[*][B]Double-chest ready[/B]: Listings automatically bind to both sides of a double chest and refresh their signs whenever stock changes so the status is always accurate.
[/LIST]

[B][COLOR=#00bfff] How to open a player shop[/COLOR][/B]
[LIST=1]
[*][B]Preset your values (optional)[/B]: Run [icode]/playershop[/icode] to open the setup menu. Use the +/- buttons to lock in a quantity and price that respect your configured limits; the plugin saves these until you change them again.
[*][B]Stock a chest[/B]: Place the item you want to sell inside the chest (or both sides of a double chest) so EzShops can detect the template stack.
[*][B]Add the sign[/B]: Attach a sign to the chest and write [icode][playershop][/icode] (or another allowed header) on the first line.
[*][B]Enter quantity and price[/B]: Fill in the second line with the amount to sell per purchase (e.g. [icode]x16[/icode]) and the third line with the total cost (numbers only). Leave either line blank to reuse the values you saved with [icode]/playershop[/icode].
[*][B]Let EzShops verify[/B]: When you place the sign, the plugin checks ownership, chest stock, and any price or quantity guards before rewriting the sign with your themed formatting.
[*][B]Maintain stock[/B]: Keep the chest supplied; EzShops instantly flags the sign as out of stock and flips it back when you restock or close the chest inventory.
[*][B]Collect earnings[/B]: Every sale deposits money into your account, notifies you if you are online, and keeps the sign synced with the remaining stock.
[/LIST]

[B][COLOR=#00bfff] ShopPriceService API examples[/COLOR][/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]Lookup the service[/B]
[code=java]
RegisteredServiceProvider<ShopPriceService> provider = Bukkit.getServicesManager().getRegistration(ShopPriceService.class);
ShopPriceService prices = provider != null ? provider.getProvider() : null;
[/code]
[*][B]Query buy and sell totals[/B]
[code=java]
ItemStack stack = new ItemStack(Material.DIAMOND, 16);
prices.findBuyPrice(stack).ifPresent(total -> player.sendMessage("Buy price: " + total));
prices.findSellPrice(stack).ifPresent(total -> player.sendMessage("Sell price: " + total));
[/code]
[*][B]Cache your reference[/B]: Grab the provider during plugin enable and reuse it for commands, GUIs, and scheduled tasks.
[/LIST]

[B][COLOR=#00bfff] Quick start[/COLOR][/B]
[LIST]
[*]Install Vault and an economy provider like [URL='https://www.spigotmc.org/resources/1-21-ezeconomy-modern-vault-economy-plugin-for-minecraft-servers.130975/']EzEconomy[/URL], then drop [icode]EzShops.jar[/icode] into [icode]plugins/[/icode].
[*]Restart the server to generate default shop categories, sign formats, and dynamic pricing storage.
[*]Edit [icode]plugins/EzShops/shop.yml[/icode] (or the files under [icode]plugins/EzShops/shop/[/icode]) to tailor categories, prices, and display copy.
[*]Grant [icode]ezshops.shop.sign.create[/icode] to trusted builders so they can post buy/sell signs around your spawn.
[/LIST]

